{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
In a [G]cavern, in a canyon,
Excavating for a [D]mine,
Dwelt a miner, forty-[G]niner,
And his [D]daughter Clemen[G]tine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
{x_strum: D - D U D U}
Oh my [G]darling, oh my darling,
Oh my darling Clemen[D]tine,
You are lost and gone for[G]ever,
Dreadful [D]sorry, Clemen[G]tine.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
Light she [G]was and like a fairy,
And her shoes were number [D]nine,
Herring boxes without [G]topses,
Sandals [D]were for Clemen[G]tine.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Drove she [G]ducklings to the water
Every morning just at [D]nine,
Hit her foot against a [G]splinter,
Fell in[D]to the foaming [G]brine.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}
Ruby [G]lips above the water,
Blowing bubbles soft and [D]fine,
But alas, I was no [G]swimmer,
So I [D]lost my Clemen[G]tine.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
